# Specify Plugin - Specify Workflow

## Overview

This plugin provides the core Specify workflow skills: initialize a project, plan a change, refine slices, build them, merge completed slices, drop discarded slices, and finalize. Each skill is an ultrathin wrapper that invokes the matching `specify` CLI verb and relays its output; the drained execute loop is the guest-routed `specify plan execute` verb, with no skill wrapper.

**Purpose**: Drive the `plan -> execute` rhythm (which itself drives `refine -> build -> merge` per slice), with `drop` for cleanup and `finalize` for closing.

## Source / target adapter structure

Adapters split into two roles:

- **Source adapters** (`adapters/sources/<name>/`) supply input — `survey` (plan time) and `extract` (slice time). Examples: `intent`, `documentation`, `typescript`, `screenshots`.
- **Target adapters** (`adapters/targets/<name>/`) consume artifacts — `guidance`, `build`, and `merge`. Examples: `omnia`, `vectis`, `contracts`.

Each directory contains operation prompts under `prose/prompts/`; adapter identity and metadata come from the compiled component (`describe`), not a manifest file.

## Slice lifecycle

Slices track lifecycle in `metadata.yaml`. The fixed loop is `refine -> build -> merge`, with `drop` as the rollback path:

```text
refining -> refined -> built -> merged
    \          \         \
     `--------> `-------> `-------> dropped
```

- **refining**: Slice directory created; `/spec:refine` extract + synthesis in flight
- **refined**: Proposal, spec, design, and tasks are validated
- **built**: All tasks done, ready to merge
- **merged**: Delta specs merged into baseline, slice archived
- **dropped**: Slice archived without merging into baseline

Per-entry `pending` / `in-progress` / `done` lives in `plan.yaml`, not `metadata.yaml`.

## Workflow

```text
/spec:init <target>               (once per project; for a registry-only workspace, use specify init --workspace)

/spec:plan <name> source ...      (authors change.md + plan.yaml; exits at lifecycle: pending)

specify plan transition <name> approved   (Gate 1; operator-only)

specify plan execute              (guest-routed loop: refine -> build -> merge per slice)

/spec:finalize <name>             (confirm publication, archive plan)
```

Breakouts invoke the same guest orchestrations one slice at a time, when the execute loop parks or the operator wants to drive a slice by hand:

- **/spec:refine**: For one slice — extract per source, synthesize `proposal.md` / `specs/<domain>/spec.md` / `design.md` / `tasks.md`, validate, transition to `refined` (`specify slice refine`).
- **/spec:build**: Build one slice through its target adapter (`specify slice build`).
- **/spec:merge**: Fold a slice's deltas into the baseline and archive it (`specify slice merge run`).
- **/spec:drop**: Abandon a slice without merging (`specify slice drop`).

## Troubleshooting

### Project not initialized

- Run `/spec:init <target>` in the project root to create `.specify/` and write `project.yaml`
- Verify `.specify/project.yaml` exists

### Slice not found

- Inspect `.specify/slices/` to see active slices
- Check the slice name matches (kebab-case)

### Artifacts incomplete

- Run `specify slice validate <name>` to check artifact status
- Re-run `/spec:refine <name>` to regenerate artifacts for one slice
- Re-run `/spec:plan <name> ...` to author a fresh change

